                <pb facs="0291" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A.R.–N.C./31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-02-01T19:00:00-05:00">February 1, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. Referring to the Department’s circular dated January 27, 3 p.m., Minister of
                    Foreign Relations assures me Colombian Government likewise believes Neutrality
                    Committee [competent?] to study, coordinate and make recommendations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
